  "body": "Closes #5871.\n\nDecision record for talk-page semantics, settling the four questions #5682 §2 leaves open. Design only — no implementation code.\n\n**Decisions**\n1. **Creation — lazy.** A talk page exists only as the `talk_for` binding on the first signed post; an undiscussed object costs zero storage and exposes no artifact. Clients may offer \"start the discussion\" to any object reader; nothing is pre-created.\n2. **Permissions — intersection, narrowing-only.** `can_read(talk_page) = can_read(object) ∧ is_member(conversation)`. No override may widen past object read-authority. Cross-object threads intersect over *all* anchors. Hard rule: no content **or existence** leak — for a non-reader the page is indistinguishable from an object with no talk page.\n3. **Lifecycle.** Archive makes posting fail at admission (architectural, not client-side); ownership transfer moves binding/governance authority with the object without re-binding; object tombstone **preserves** the conversation, folds the binding to `orphaned`, removes the object-side entry point, and never re-adopts the page on object re-creation; `talk_for` targeting a conversation is rejected so recursion is depth one.\n4. **Moderation and binding — split.** Object owner governs structure (lock/close/pin/announce/slow) via signed events; server moderation (#835) retains takedown, implemented as signed events, never deletes. Only the object owner or an owner-named delegate may bind; unauthorized bindings are rejected at admission (disputed is for legitimate conflicts only).\n5. **Mapping to existing code.** Membership is the object read set projected through group policy (`pkgs/id/src/groups/policy.rs`); `History::Full` for unconditional audiences, `History::FromJoin` when read-authority is granted per key, `Recent(n)` only to tighten. Revocation cannot un-deliver — stated as the design's one honest limitation, with key rotation left to #5801.\n\n**Explicitly recorded for parents/siblings:** #5682 §2 is preserved and only refined (the read-authority sentence is read as intersection + narrowing); #5872 is unchanged — this record supplies the binding authority and visibility intersection it delegated; #5870/#835/#5873/#5874/#5875 untouched. If #5682 intended \"any object reader reads every thread regardless of membership\", that is a parent change and is flagged rather than made silently.\n\nNine testable invariants are in §6 (intersection at read time, no-existence-leak indistinguishability, narrowing-only as a property test, lazy equivalence, depth one, preservation, authority determinism, architectural archive, total history mapping).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796819328&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8041&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8041&signature=ed1617a553c1c37c5ff881d848ea85d384f60baee26b712883937807832fff3b\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8041?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
